{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792611704,"nonce":"Ba5rZkve2BOAfAcVJvZO33GXn7M=","title":"TypeScript: align parser and semantic diagnostic categories with the reference checker","message":"The native Oxc parser reports several TypeScript semantic/grammar errors as Syntax, causing genuine category mismatches even though both checkers reject the source.\n\nMinimal reproducer: const x;\nTypeScript: Type, TS1155 and TS7005. zynode: exit 1, Syntax, Missing initializer in const declaration.\n\nThe initial whole-corpus pass also exposes Cannot assign to this expression, invalid class/modifier combinations, invalid for-of declarations, yield-context errors and ambient declaration errors. Some are parse-versus-semantic classification differences; others need source-mode handling. Classify deliberately rather than converting every rejection into a compatibility pass. Check diagnostic priority when the source contains multiple errors. Cases with real syntax errors must retain Syntax.\n\nReproducible harness retains exact reference diagnostics and native messages; only acceptance/category is currently compared.\n\nEvidence: official TypeScript conformance corpus at 3e9236361fa97a9e6c685f4833ac457ae2d8c50a, oracle 7.1.0-beta, native d978fe3fa5f8f7480d0c0d1b7dd2ca4548b490f0. This is check-only acceptance/category comparison under strict defaults, not JIT/runtime coverage. The full affected-case inventory will be attached after the complete audited run. Parent: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5.","files":null}]}